[2026-04-14T07:54:24.703Z] [INFO]         "type": "tool_result",
[2026-04-14T07:54:24.703Z] [INFO]         "content": "1\t# Doublets\n2\t\n3\t[![CI](https://github.com/linksplatform/doublets-rs/workflows/CI/badge.svg)](https://github.com/linksplatform/doublets-rs/actions?query=workflow%3ACI+branch%3Amain)\n4\t[![Benchmark](https://github.com/linksplatform/doublets-rs/workflows/Benchmark/badge.svg)](https://github.com/linksplatform/doublets-rs/actions?query=workflow%3ABenchmark+branch%3Amain)\n5\t[![Crates.io](https://img.shields.io/crates/v/doublets.svg)](https://crates.io/crates/doublets)\n6\t[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-Unlicense-blue.svg)](https://github.com/linksplatform/doublets-rs/blob/main/LICENSE)\n7\t\n8\tLinksPlatform's Rust implementation of Doublets (associative storage links).\n9\t\n10\tRust port of [Data.Doublets](https://github.com/linksplatform/Data.Doublets) library.\n11\t\n12\t## Overview\n13\t\n14\tDoublets is an associative data structure that represents a link store where each link consists of:\n15\t- **Index** - unique identifier of the link\n16\t- **Source** - the link's source (can reference itself or another link)\n17\t- **Target** - the link's target (can reference itself or another link)\n18\t\n19\tThis simple yet powerful structure can represent any data model, from traditional key-value pairs to complex graph structures. Doublets provide a unified approach to data storage with constant-time lookup operations using size-balanced trees.\n20\t\n21\t### Key Features\n22\t\n23\t- **File-mapped storage** - data persists directly to disk using memory-mapped files\n24\t- **Generic link types** - supports any unsigned integer type (`u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `usize`)\n25\t- **Two storage modes**:\n26\t  - `unit::Store` - combined data and index storage in a single memory region\n27\t  - `split::Store` - separated data and index storage for optimized memory layouts\n28\t- **Thread-safe** - `Send` and `Sync` implementations for concurrent access\n29\t- **Query system** - flexible pattern matching using `any` constants\n30\t- **FFI bindings** - C-compatible foreign function interface for cross-language integration\n31\t\n32\t## Installation\n33\t\n34\tAdd to your `Cargo.toml`:\n35\t\n36\t```toml\n37\t[dependencies]\n38\tdoublets = \"0.1.0-pre\"\n39\t```\n40\t\n41\t**Note:** This crate requires nightly Rust due to usage of experimental features.\n42\t\n43\t```bash\n44\trustup default nightly\n45\t```\n46\t\n47\t## Example\n48\t\n49\tBasic CRUD operations with doublets:\n50\t\n51\t```rust\n52\tuse doublets::{mem, unit, Doublets, DoubletsExt, Link, Links};\n53\tuse data::Flow;\n54\t\n55\tfn main() -> Result<(), doublets::Error<usize>> {\n56\t    // Use file as persistent storage for doublets\n57\t    let mem = mem::FileMapped::from_path(\"db.links\")?;\n58\t    let mut store = unit::Store::<usize, _>::new(mem)?;\n59\t\n60\t    // Create a point link (a link that references itself as both source and target)\n61\t    // Point: 1 -> (1, 1)\n62\t    let point = store.create_point()?;\n63\t    println!(\"Created point: {}\", point);\n64\t\n65\t    // Create a regular link with explicit source and target\n66\t    // Link: 2 -> (1, 1)\n67\t    let link = store.create_link(point, point)?;\n68\t    println!(\"Created link: {}\", link);\n69\t\n70\t    // The `any` constant matches any link in queries\n71\t    let any = store.constants().any;\n72\t\n73\t    // Count all links in the store\n74\t    println!(\"Total links: {}\", store.count());\n75\t\n76\t    // Iterate over all links using pattern [any, any, any]\n77\t    println!(\"All links:\");\n78\t    store.each_iter([any, any, any]).for_each(|link| {\n79\t        println!(\"  {}: {} -> {}\", link.index, link.source, link.target);\n80\t    });\n81\t\n82\t    // Query links by source: find all links where source = point\n83\t    println!(\"Links with source = {}:\", point);\n84\t    store.each_iter([any, point, any]).for_each(|link| {\n85\t        println!(\"  {}: {} -> {}\", link.index, link.source, link.target);\n86\t    });\n87\t\n88\t    // Update a link: change the target\n89\t    let updated = store.update(link, point, link)?;\n90\t    println!(\"Updated link {} to target {}\", link, updated);\n91\t\n92\t    // Delete a link with a callback handler\n93\t    store.delete_with(link, |before, after| {\n94\t        println!(\"Deleted: {:?} => {:?}\", before, after);\n95\t        Flow::Continue\n96\t    })?;\n97\t\n98\t    // Clean up: delete all remaining links\n99\t    store.delete_all()?;\n100\t\n101\t    Ok(())\n102\t}\n103\t```\n104\t\n105\t### Using In-Memory Storage\n106\t\n107\tFor testing or temporary data, you can use heap-allocated memory instead of file storage:\n108\t\n109\t```rust\n110\tuse doublets::{mem, unit, Doublets, Links};\n111\t\n112\tfn main() -> Result<(), doublets::Error<usize>> {\n113\t    // Use global allocator for in-memory storage\n114\t    let mem = mem::Global::new();\n115\t    let mut store = unit::Store::<usize, _>::new(mem)?;\n116\t\n117\t    // Create some links\n118\t    for i in 0..100 {\n119\t        store.create_point()?;\n120\t    }\n121\t\n122\t    println!(\"Created {} links\", store.count());\n123\t    Ok(())\n124\t}\n125\t```\n126\t\n127\t### Using Split Storage\n128\t\n129\tSplit storage separates data and index trees for potentially better cache utilization:\n130\t\n131\t```rust\n132\tuse doublets::{split::Store, Doublets, Links};\n133\tuse mem::Global;\n134\t\n135\tfn main() -> Result<(), doublets::Error<usize>> {\n136\t    let mut store = Store::<usize, _, _>::new(Global::new(), Global::new())?;\n137\t\n138\t    // Create 1 million point links\n139\t    for _ in 0..1_000_000 {\n140\t        store.create_point()?;\n141\t    }\n142\t\n143\t    println!(\"Total links: {}\", store.count());\n144\t    Ok(())\n145\t}\n146\t```\n147\t\n148\t## API Overview\n149\t\n150\t### Core Traits\n151\t\n152\t| Trait | Description |\n153\t|-------|-------------|\n154\t| `Links<T>` | Low-level CRUD operations with handlers |\n155\t| `Doublets<T>` | High-level operations with ergonomic API |\n156\t| `DoubletsExt<T>` | Iterator extensions and parallel processing |\n157\t\n158\t### Main Types\n159\t\n160\t| Type | Description |\n161\t|------|-------------|\n162\t| `Link<T>` | A triplet of (index, source, target) |\n163\t| `Doublet<T>` | A pair of (source, target) without index |\n164\t| `unit::Store` | Combined memory layout storage |\n165\t| `split::Store` | Separated memory layout storage |\n166\t| `Error<T>` | Error type for link operations |\n167\t\n168\t### Key Operations\n169\t\n170\t```rust\n171\t// Create operations\n172\tstore.create()?;                      // Create empty link\n173\tstore.create_point()?;                // Create self-referencing link\n174\tstore.create_link(source, target)?;   // Create link with source and target\n175\t\n176\t// Read operations\n177\tstore.count();                        // Count all links\n178\tstore.count_by([any, source, any]);   // Count by pattern\n179\tstore.get_link(index);                // Get link by index\n180\tstore.search(source, target);         // Find link by source and target\n181\tstore.iter();                         // Iterate all links\n182\tstore.each_iter(query);               // Iterate by pattern\n183\t\n184\t// Update operations\n185\tstore.update(index, source, target)?; // Update link\n186\t\n187\t// Delete operations\n188\tstore.delete(index)?;                 // Delete link\n189\tstore.delete_all()?;                  // Delete all links\n190\t```\n191\t\n192\t## Architecture\n193\t\n194\t```\n195\tdoublets-rs/\n196\t├── doublets/           # Core library\n197\t│   ├── src/\n198\t│   │   ├── data/       # Core data structures (Link, Doublet, traits)\n199\t│   │   └── mem/        # Memory management and storage\n200\t│   │       ├── unit/   # Combined storage implementation\n201\t│   │       └── split/  # Split storage implementation\n202\t│   └── benches/        # Performance benchmarks\n203\t├── doublets-ffi/       # C FFI bindings\n204\t├── dev-deps/           # Platform dependencies\n205\t│   ├── data-rs/        # Data primitives (LinkType, Flow, etc.)\n206\t│   ├── mem-rs/         # Memory abstractions (RawMem, FileMapped)\n207\t│   └── trees-rs/       # Tree structures (size-balanced trees)\n208\t└── integration/        # Integration tests\n209\t```\n210\t\n211\t## Features\n212\t\n213\t| Feature | Description |\n214\t|---------|-------------|\n215\t| `platform` (default) | Core platform types and traits |\n216\t| `mem` | Memory management utilities |\n217\t| `num` | Numeric utilities |\n218\t| `data` | Re-exports from `platform-data` |\n219\t| `rayon` | Parallel iteration support |\n220\t| `small-search` | Stack-allocated buffers for small queries |\n221\t| `full` | All features enabled |\n222\t\n223\t## Performance\n224\t\n225\tThe library is optimized for high-throughput operations:\n226\t\n227\t- **Size-balanced trees** for O(log n) search, insert, and delete operations\n228\t- **Memory-mapped files** for efficient disk I/O\n229\t- **Optional parallel iteration** with rayon feature\n230\t- Benchmarks show creation of 1 million points in ~1 second on modern hardware\n231\t\n232\tRun benchmarks:\n233\t\n234\t```bash\n235\tcargo bench --all-features\n236\t```\n237\t\n238\t## Related Projects\n239\t\n240\t- [Data.Doublets](https://github.com/linksplatform/Data.Doublets) - C# implementation\n241\t- [Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets](https://github.com/linksplatform/Comparisons.SQLiteVSDoublets) - Performance comparison with SQLite\n242\t\n243\t## Documentation\n244\t\n245\t- [API Documentation](https://docs.rs/doublets) (when published)\n246\t- [LinksPlatform Overview](https://github.com/linksplatform)\n247\t\n248\t## Dependencies\n249\t\n250\t- [platform-data](https://github.com/linksplatform/data-rs) - Core data types\n251\t- [platform-mem](https://github.com/linksplatform/mem-rs) - Memory abstractions\n252\t- [platform-trees](https://github.com/linksplatform/trees-rs) - Tree implementations\n253\t\n254\t## Support\n255\t\n256\t- Ask questions at [stackoverflow.com/tags/links-platform](https://stackoverflow.com/tags/links-platform) (use tag `links-platform`)\n257\t- Join our [Discord server](https://discord.gg/eEXJyjWv5e) for real-time support\n258\t- Open issues on [GitHub](https://github.com/linksplatform/doublets-rs/issues)\n259\t\n260\t## License\n261\t\n262\tThis project is released into the public domain under the [Unlicense](LICENSE).\n263\t"
