ile on stable Rust\",\n40327:[2026-04-13T10:22:34.433Z] [INFO]               \"activeForm\": \"Removing nightly features for stable Rust\"\n40411:[2026-04-13T10:22:34.446Z] [INFO]         \"content\": \"Remove nightly features and pin to stable Rust toolchain\",\n40413:[2026-04-13T10:22:34.446Z] [INFO]         \"activeForm\": \"Removing nightly features and pinning to stable Rust toolchain\"\n40416:[2026-04-13T10:22:34.446Z] [INFO]         \"content\": \"Replace git submodule dependencies with crates.io packages\",\n40473:[2026-04-13T10:22:34.446Z] [INFO]         \"content\": \"Migrate platform dependencies from submodules to crates.io packages\",\n40493:[2026-04-13T10:22:34.446Z] [INFO]         \"content\": \"Remove nightly features and make code compile on stable Rust\",\n40495:[2026-04-13T10:22:34.446Z] [INFO]         \"activeForm\": \"Removing nightly features for stable Rust\"\n44604:[2026-04-13T10:25:59.744Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"The new `platform-data` main branch has `Flow` **without** `Try` impl - it's stable Rust compatible. The old submodule's `Flow` implements `Try` (nightly). This means:\\n\\n1. The `handler(link)?` pattern in store code that relies on `Flow: Try` needs to change to explicit match/if\\n2. The `Doublets` trait methods using `R: Try<Output = ()>` need rethinking\\n\\nLet me also check the new data-rs Links trait and handlers.\"\n45643:[2026-04-13T10:26:46.657Z] [INFO]         \"text\": \"The submodule (SHA 95b7d4d) is the old code I already have locally. The crates.io v0.1.0-beta.3 is from the same era and uses nightly.\\n\\nSince the main branches of all three platform crates have been updated to stable Rust but not yet released to crates.io (except mem 0.3.0 and trees 0.3.3 which are recent), I should use the latest crates.io versions. Let me check if platform-data has a newer version on main that hasn't been published.\"\n45906:[Omitted long matching line]\n45945:[Omitted long matching line]\n45980:[Omitted long matching line]\n45991:[Omitted long matching line]\n55421:[Omitted long matching line]\n55433:[Omitted long matching line]\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 40]"
