ion: `changelog.d/` directory\n- Format: Markdown with YAML frontmatter\n\n**Sample Fragment Structure:**\n```yaml\n---\nbump: minor\n---\n\n### Added\n- Feature description\n\n### Changed\n- Change description\n```\n\n**Allowed bump types:**\n- `patch` - bug fixes, backward compatible\n- `minor` - new features, backward compatible\n- `major` - breaking changes\n\n**Workflow Integration:**\n- PRs with code changes MUST include changelog fragment\n- Docs-only PRs exempt from changelog requirement\n- Scripts detect changes (rs, toml, docs, workflows)\n- `get-bump-type.rs` determines version bump from fragments\n- `collect-changelog.rs` consolidates fragments into CHANGELOG.md\n- `check-version-modification.rs` prevents manual version edits in PRs\n\n---\n\n### 4. **RUST PROJECT CONFIGURATIONS**\n\n#### mem-rs (linksplatform/mem-rs)\n- **Edition**: 2024 (latest)\n- **MSRV**: 1.85\n- **License**: Unlicense\n- **Key Dependencies**: allocator-api2, memmap2, tempfile, thiserror, tokio (optional)\n- **Profiles**: LTO enabled, single codegen unit, stripped binaries in release\n- **Lint Config**: Comprehensive clippy allowances with documented exceptions\n\n#### trees-rs (linksplatform/trees-rs)\n- **Edition**: 2024 (latest)\n- **MSRV**: 1.85\n- **License**: Unlicense\n- **Key Dependencies**: num-traits, platform-num\n- **Profiles**: LTO enabled, single codegen unit, stripped binaries\n- **Lint Config**: Similar clippy configuration\n\n#### Numbers (linksplatform/Numbers)\n- **Edition**: 2024 (latest)\n- **MSRV**: 1.85\n- **License**: Unlicense\n- **Package**: platform-num\n- **Key Dependencies**: num-traits\n- **Profiles**: Optimized for size/performance\n\n#### rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\n- **Edition**: 2021\n- **MSRV**: 1.70 (lowest)\n- **License**: Unlicense\n- **Includes**: Binary + library dual support\n- **Key Dependencies**: clap, lino-arguments\n- **Lint Config**: `forbid unsafe_code` (stricter than others)\n- **Notable**: Template-aware safety checks (skips publishing for example-sum-package-name)\n\n#### Shared rust-toolchain.toml Pattern:\n```toml\n[toolchain]\nchannel = \"stable\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. **RELEASE & PUBLISHING**\n\n**Automation Workflow:**\n- **Auto-release**: Triggered on push to main after successful tests\n- **Instant Release**: Manual workflow_dispatch with bump type selection\n- **Changelog PR**: Creates PR for review before release (optional mode)\n\n**Publishing Steps:**\n1. Version bump (determined by changelog fragments)\n2. Build release binary (`cargo build --release`)\n3. Publish to crates.io\n4. Create GitHub Release with changelog\n5. Deploy documentation to GitHub Pages\n\n**Environment Variables:**\n```yaml\nCARGO_TERM_COLOR: always\nRUSTFLAGS: -Dwarnings\nCARGO_TOKEN: secrets.CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN || secrets.CARGO_TOKEN\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. **CODE QUALITY & TESTING**\n\n**Lint Stage:**\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` (formatting)\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features` (linting with -D warnings)\n- `rust-script scripts/check-file-size.rs` (size limits)\n- `rust-script scripts/check-version-modification.rs` (version protection)\n\n**Test Stage:**\n- Multi-platform testing: ubuntu-latest, macos-latest, windows-latest\n- `cargo test --all-features --verbose`\n- `cargo test --doc --verbose` (doc tests)\n- Uses fail-fast: false for comprehensive results\n\n**Cache Strategy:**\n- Paths: `~/.cargo/registry`, `~/.cargo/git`, `target/`\n- Key: `${{ runner.os }}-cargo-${{ hashFiles('**/Cargo.lock') }}`\n- Restore keys for partial hits\n\n**Pre-commit Hooks** (in template):\n```yaml\n- cargo fmt --all\n- cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings\n- cargo test\n- Pre-commit hooks from standard library (trailing whitespace, YAML validation, etc.)\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. **DOCUMENTATION GENERATION**\n\n**Approach:**\n- Uses `cargo doc --no-deps` for rustdoc generation\n- Deployed via `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages@v4`\n- Published to GitHub Pages under `rust/` subdirectory\n- Keeps existing files (`keep_files: true`)\n\n**Supporting Files:**\n- README.md (primary documentation)\n- CONTRIBUTING.md (contributor guidelines)\n- CHANGELOG.md (generated from fragments)\n- docs/ directory for case studies and guides\n\n**No mdbook setup** - repositories rely on:\n- Rustdoc for API documentation\n- README for project overview\n- CONTRIBUTING for development workflow\n- docs/ for guides/case studies\n\n---\n\n### 8. **HELPER SCRIPTS (Rust-based in template)**\n\nLocated in `scripts/` directory, all implemented as `.rs` files runnable via `rust-script`:\n\n1. **detect-code-changes.rs** - Determines what changed (rs, toml, docs, workflow files)\n2. **check-changelog-fragment.rs** - Validates changelog fragment added in PR diff\n3. **check-version-modification.rs** - Prevents manual version changes\n4. **get-bump-type.rs** - Determines version bump from fragments\n5. **check-release-needed.rs** - Checks if release should proceed\n6. **collect-changelog.rs** - Consolidates fragments into CHANGELOG.md\n7. **version-and-commit.rs** - Bumps version and commits\n8. **get-version.rs** - Reads current version from Cargo.toml\n9. **publish-crate.rs** - Publishes to crates.io with version validation\n10. **create-github-release.rs** - Creates GitHub release with changelog\n11. **git-config.rs** - Configures git for CI operations\n12. **create-changelog-fragment.rs** - Creates new fragments for manual releases\n13. **bump-version.rs** - Version manipulation utility\n\n---\n\n### 9. **KEY BEST PRACTICES IDENTIFIED**\n\n1. **Deterministic Change Detection**: Each job runs conditionally based on what actually changed\n2. **Fragment-based Versioning**: Enforces changelog discipline without manual version management\n3. **Multi-platform Testing**: Validates across Ubuntu, macOS, Windows\n4. **Protected Main Branch**: Version changes only via automated pipeline\n5. **Cargo.lock Caching**: Efficient cache invalidation with Cargo.lock hash\n6. **Documentation Pipeline**: Auto-generated and deployed on releases\n7. **Semantic Versioning**: Enforced through controlled bump types\n8. **Script Portability**: Using Rust scripts for cross-platform compatibility\n9. **Token Management**: Fallback support for both CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN and CARGO_TOKEN\n10. **Workspace Safety**: Template includes checks to prevent accidental publishing with example names\n\n---\n\n### 10. **FILE LOCATIONS REFERENCE**\n\n**All repos share this structure:**\n```\n.\n├── .github/workflows/\n│   └── release.yml (or ci.yml)\n├── .pre-commit-config.yaml (template)\n├── rust-toolchain.toml (mem-rs, trees-rs only)\n├── Cargo.toml\n├── Cargo.lock\n├── scripts/\n│   └── *.rs (multiple helper scripts)\n├── changelog.d/\n│   └── *.md (fragments)\n├── src/\n├── tests/\n├── docs/\n│   ├── case-studies/\n│   └── ci-cd/ (template only)\n├── README.md\n├── CONTRIBUTING.md\n└── CHANGELOG.md\n```\n\nAll findings have been documented from direct API exploration of these reference repositories. The template at `link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template` serves as the most complete reference implementation with all these practices fully documented and implemented."
