[2026-04-14T07:57:45.316Z] [INFO]         "text": "This is very important. The `data-rs` crate itself uses many nightly features (`try_trait_v2`, `const_trait_impl`, `step_trait`, `associated_type_bounds`, etc.). The latest `platform-data` on crates.io is `0.1.0-beta.3` from 2022, which also uses nightly features. But `platform-mem` 0.3.0 and `platform-trees` 0.3.3 are recent and work with stable Rust.\n\nThe key challenge is that `platform-data` defines `Flow`, `LinkType`, `LinksConstants`, etc. - all core types. Since `platform-data` on crates.io is outdated and uses nightly, I need to check if the latest `platform-data` on GitHub's main branch has been updated."
