[2026-04-14T08:00:16.549Z] [INFO]         "text": "`Fuse` is used as `Fuse::new(handler)` and then passed to methods like `self.delete_with(index, &mut handler)?` and `self.update_with(new, source, target, handler)`. These methods expect `F: FnMut(Link<T>, Link<T>) -> R` where `R: Try<Output = ()>`.\n\nThe cleanest approach is to:\n1. Remove the `Handler` and `Fuse` types entirely since they relied on nightly features\n2. Simplify the `Doublets` trait to use `Flow` directly instead of generic `R: Try<Output = ()>`\n3. Replace `handler(link)?` with explicit `is_break()` checks\n\nThis is a major simplification but keeps the same functionality. The `Try` trait was only used to allow both `Flow` and `ControlFlow<()>` as handler return types - but since `Flow` is the only type actually used in practice, we can simplify.\n\nLet me check if any external code uses the generic `R: Try` parameter."
[2026-04-14T08:00:16.549Z] [INFO]       }
