[2026-04-14T08:02:25.239Z] [INFO]         "text": "In the repository at /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1776153218771, I need to replace all uses of the `?` operator on `Flow` type with explicit `is_break()` checks in the unit store tree files. The `Flow` type no longer implements the `Try` trait.\n\nThe pattern to replace in functions returning `Flow`:\n- `handler(link)?;` becomes `if handler(link).is_break() { return Flow::Break; }`  \n- `each_usages_core(...)?;` becomes `if each_usages_core(...).is_break() { return Flow::Break; }`\n- `self.each_core(handler, &[...])?;` becomes `if self.each_core(handler, &[...]).is_break() { return Flow::Break; }`\n\nFiles to update (all in doublets/src/mem/unit/):\n1. `generic/sources_recursionless_size_balanced_tree.rs` - the `each_usages_core` function and `each_usages` method\n2. `generic/targets_recursionless_size_balanced_tree.rs` - same pattern\n3. `store.rs` - the `each_core` method and `handler(link)?` calls\n\nAlso in these files:\n- Remove `use std::ops::Try;` if present\n- Replace `use std::default::default;` / `default()` calls with `Default::default()` or `T::funty(0)` as appropriate\n- Replace `NonNull::slice_from_raw_parts(NonNull::dangling(), 0)` with `NonNull::from(&mut [] as &mut [_])` or equivalent stable construct\n\nFor store.rs specifically:\n- The old `RawMem<T>` trait had `alloc(capacity) -> Result<&mut [T]>` and `allocated() -> usize` \n- Keep the current old-style RawMem API for now (we'll migrate the mem dependency separately)\n\nMake ALL the changes needed. Read each file first, then edit it. Commit nothing - just make the edits."
