[2026-04-14T08:06:35.889Z] [INFO]         "text": "The problem is that `trees::RecursiveSizeBalancedTree<T>` requires `T: trees::LinkType` which requires `T: Number + Unsigned + TryFrom<u8> + FromPrimitive`. But our doublets code uses `T: data::LinkType` which requires `T: Unsigned + FuntyPart + ...`. These are different trait bounds.\n\nThe new `trees` crate uses its own `LinkType` from `platform-num::Number`. These are incompatible trait bounds.\n\nI need to check: do the standard unsigned types (`u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `usize`) satisfy BOTH `data::LinkType` and `trees::LinkType`? If yes, then since we only ever instantiate with those concrete types, it should work.\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully, the `trees` traits take generic `T: trees::LinkType`. But in the doublets code, when we do `impl<T: data::LinkType> RecursiveSizeBalancedTree<T> for ...`, the compiler needs to verify that `T: trees::LinkType` too. Since `data::LinkType` and `trees::LinkType` have different supertraits, this won't compile.\n\nI need a different approach. Let me check if the new `data-rs` on GitHub main also uses `trees::LinkType` or if it's independent.\n\nLooking at the `data-rs` main branch `link_type.rs`, it defines `LinkType` as: `Unsigned + FuntyPart + TryFrom<many types>`. The `trees` crate defines `LinkType` as: `Number + Unsigned + TryFrom<u8> + FromPrimitive`.\n\nFor this to work, I need to either:\n1. Add `trees::LinkType` as an additional bound in the doublets code where tree traits are used\n2. Or keep the old trees-rs submodule that uses `data::LinkType`\n\nOption 2 is simpler. But the old trees-rs uses nightly features.\n\nLet me check the latest trees-rs on GitHub main to see if it still uses `data::LinkType`:"
