[2026-04-14T08:08:15.257Z] [INFO]         "text": "The new API is grow-only (add `cap` elements), not resize-to-capacity. The old `alloc(capacity)` resizes to exactly `capacity` elements.\n\nThe cleanest approach: define a local `RawMem` compatibility trait (or keep our own version of the old trait). Actually wait - the doublets crate defined `RawMem` as an external dependency from `mem`. I need to bridge the gap.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The stores in doublets need a memory backend. Instead of depending on the external `platform-mem` crate's trait, I can define a simple trait in doublets itself that matches what the stores need, and then provide impls for `platform-mem` types.\n\nActually, the simplest approach: keep the old `RawMem` trait definition locally in doublets, provide an adapter for the new `platform-mem` types, and update exports.\n\nBut actually, looking at the issue requirements again: \"We should depend on real cargo/crates packages, not source code.\" The intent is to use crates.io packages. The new `platform-mem` 0.3.0 has a different API. I should adapt the store code to use the new API.\n\nLet me write the adaptation. The key changes needed in the stores:\n\nOld pattern → New pattern:\n- `mem.alloc(cap)` (resize to cap) → need `grow_zeroed(cap - allocated().len())` when growing\n- `mem.allocated()` (returns `usize`) → `mem.allocated().len()`\n- `NonNull::from(mem.alloc(cap)?)` → `NonNull::from(unsafe { mem.grow_zeroed(cap)? })`\n\nLet me also check what `mem::Error` maps to for the doublets error type:"
