[2026-04-14T08:10:52.439Z] [INFO]         "text": "Now for the `LinkType` trait bound issue. The fundamental problem is that `data::LinkType` and `trees::LinkType` have incompatible requirements. I need to add `trees::LinkType` as an additional bound on `T` wherever tree traits are used.\n\nThe simplest approach: create a combined trait bound in doublets. Let me add `num-traits` as a dependency and add the bound.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the `data::LinkType` from the updated main branch: it uses `funty::Unsigned`. The `trees::LinkType` uses `num_traits::Unsigned`. These are different crates entirely.\n\nBut all standard unsigned types implement both `funty::Unsigned` and `num_traits::Unsigned`. So the concrete types work. The issue is only at the generic level.\n\nThe cleanest fix: everywhere we use `T: data::LinkType` and also use trees traits, add `+ trees::LinkType` bound. But that requires `num-traits` and `platform-num` as dependencies.\n\nActually, let me just add `num-traits` and `platform-num` as dependencies, then create a combined alias:"
