[2026-04-14T08:22:10.222Z] [INFO]             "text": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully retrieved the CI workflow files from the template repo. Here are the key findings:\n\n### Workflow Files\n**File:** `release.yml` (the only workflow file in the repo)\n\n### Key Details\n\n**Toolchain:**\n- Uses `dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable` (stable Rust toolchain)\n- No pinned version specified - always uses the latest stable release\n\n**Jobs (11 total):**\n1. **detect-changes** - Detects which files changed (Rust, TOML, docs, workflows) using rust-script\n2. **changelog** - Validates changelog fragments exist for code changes\n3. **version-check** - Prevents manual version modification in PRs\n4. **lint** - Runs cargo fmt and clippy checks on all targets\n5. **test** - Runs tests on matrix of OSes (Ubuntu, macOS, Windows)\n6. **coverage** - Generates LLVM code coverage and uploads to Codecov\n7. **build** - Builds release artifacts after lint and test pass\n8. **auto-release** - Automatic versioning and publishing on push to main (bumps version based on changelog fragments, publishes to crates.io, creates GitHub release)\n9. **manual-release** - Manual instant release via workflow_dispatch with bump_type and description inputs\n10. **changelog-pr** - Creates a changelog PR for manual releases\n11. **deploy-docs** - Deploys Rust documentation to GitHub Pages after successful release\n\n**Key Configuration:**\n- Concurrency group: One workflow per branch at a time\n- Caching: Uses cargo registry, git, and target caching with Cargo.lock hash keys\n- Environment vars: `CARGO_TERM_COLOR=always`, `RUSTFLAGS=-Dwarnings`, registry tokens for publishing\n- Conditional logic: Jobs depend on detect-changes to optimize CI runs\n- File size checks: Includes custom script to validate file sizes\n- Multi-platform testing: Tests on ubuntu-latest, macos-latest, windows-latest\n\n**Notable Features:**\n- Uses rust-script for custom automation (change detection, changelog management, versioning)\n- Supports both automated releases (from main) and manual releases (via workflow_dispatch)\n- Has changelog fragment system for semantic versioning\n- Conditional job execution based on which files changed"
