[2026-04-14T08:29:43.743Z] [INFO]           "command": "gh pr edit 48 --repo linksplatform/doublets-rs --title \"Port doublets to stable Rust, migrate deps to crates.io, update CI/CD\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n\nResolves #47 — Port doublets-rs from nightly Rust to stable, migrate dependencies to crates.io packages, and update CI/CD to match best practices from reference repositories.\n\n### Nightly to Stable Migration\n- Removed all 12 `#![feature(...)]` gates from the doublets crate\n- Replaced `Try` trait usage (`?` operator on `Flow`) with explicit `is_break()` checks\n- Replaced `fn_traits`/`unboxed_closures` on `Fuse` with a `.call()` method\n- Replaced `type_alias_impl_trait` with `-> impl Trait` return position (stable since Rust 1.75)\n- Replaced `default_free_fn` with `Default::default()` and `PhantomData`\n- Replaced `box_syntax` with `Box::new()`\n- Replaced `Range<T>` iteration with while loops (avoids nightly-only `Step` trait)\n- Fixed borrow checker issues by collecting iterators before mutation\n- Updated `rust-toolchain.toml` from `nightly-2022-08-22` to `stable`\n\n### Dependency Migration\n- Migrated `platform-mem` from git submodule to crates.io v0.3.0\n- Migrated `platform-trees` from git submodule to crates.io v0.3.3\n- Adapted to new `RawMem` API (`grow_filled`/`shrink` instead of `alloc`)\n- Adapted to renamed tree traits (`SzbTree` → `RecursiveSizeBalancedTree`, `NoRecurSzbTree` → `IterativeSizeBalancedTree`)\n- Resolved dual `LinkType` trait bounds between `data` and `trees` crates\n- Exported `FuntyPart` from `data-rs` for disambiguation\n- Updated `integration` crate to use `platform-mem` 0.3.0\n\n### CI/CD Pipeline\n- Replaced `ci.yml` + `benchmark.yml` with unified `release.yml` matching [template](https://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template)\n- Uses stable Rust toolchain (`dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable`)\n- Replaced JavaScript CI scripts with Rust scripts (`rust-script`)\n- Added jobs: detect-changes, version-check, changelog-pr, deploy-docs\n- Added auto-release and manual-release with crates.io publishing\n- Multi-platform testing (Ubuntu, macOS, Windows)\n- Code coverage with cargo-llvm-cov\n\n### Code Quality\n- All clippy warnings resolved (with `-D warnings`)\n- All tests pass (226+ tests across 18 test suites)\n- Formatting clean with stable `rustfmt`\n- Added `.gitignore` for build artifacts\n- Added changelog fragment for this release\n\n## Breaking Changes\n- `Fuse` no longer implements `FnMut` — use `fuse.call(before, after)` instead of `fuse(before, after)`\n- `Handler` trait removed — handlers use `FnMut(Link<T>, Link<T>) -> Flow` directly\n- Minimum Rust version is now 1.85 (stable)\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `cargo check -p doublets` passes on stable Rust\n- [x] `cargo clippy -p doublets -- -D warnings` passes\n- [x] `cargo fmt -p doublets -- --check` passes\n- [x] `cargo test -p doublets` — all 226+ tests pass\n- [x] `cargo test --workspace` — all workspace tests pass\n- [x] CI pipeline runs with new `release.yml`\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1",
