[2026-04-14T08:49:36.919Z] [INFO]           "command": "gh pr edit 48 --repo linksplatform/doublets-rs --body \"$(cat <<'PREOF'\n## Summary\n\nThis PR ports the doublets crate from nightly Rust to stable Rust, migrates dependencies from git submodules to crates.io packages, and modernizes the CI/CD pipeline.\n\n### Changes\n\n- **Stable Rust migration**: Removed all 12 nightly features (`try_trait_v2`, `fn_traits`, `unboxed_closures`, `default_free_fn`, `type_alias_impl_trait`, `box_syntax`, etc.) and replaced with stable equivalents\n- **Dependency migration**: Replaced git submodules with crates.io packages (`platform-mem` 0.3.0, `platform-trees` 0.3.3). Removed unused `mem-rs` and `trees-rs` submodules\n- **CI/CD pipeline**: New release workflow based on [rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template](https://github.com/link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template) with lint, test, coverage, build, auto-release, and deploy-docs jobs\n- **Documentation**: Added rustdoc comments to all public API types, traits, and methods. Crate-level and module-level documentation for `cargo doc` generation\n- **Case study**: Added `docs/case-studies/issue-47/` with detailed analysis\n\n### Key technical decisions\n\n- `Try` trait usage replaced with explicit `Flow::is_break()` checks\n- `fn_traits`/`unboxed_closures` on `Fuse` replaced with `.call()` method\n- `Range<T>` iteration (requires nightly `Step`) replaced with while loops\n- `data::LinkType` + `trees::LinkType` incompatibility resolved with `crate::TreesLinkType` dual bounds\n- `platform-data` still uses local path dependency (crates.io version requires nightly); `data-rs` submodule retained\n\n### Testing\n\n- All 296 tests pass on stable Rust\n- `cargo clippy` passes with `-D warnings`\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` passes\n- `cargo doc --workspace --no-deps` generates documentation without warnings\n\nCloses #47\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nPREOF\n)\" 2>&1",
